# Feature tests required

A feature is **not done** until Completeness allows it and verification passes.

## Required before claiming done

1. **Feature Completeness Review** (see `quality-feature-gate`) — disposition Proceed; Required gaps closed or deferred in writing.
2. **Challenge** platform consistency — Reject/Redesign when the ask fights Ekum philosophy.
3. **Update** `docs/features/*.md` for approved shipped behaviour.
4. **Test matrix** covering happy path, personas, and BM-* bug modes where relevant.
5. **Automate both tracks**:
   - **Regression:** API `*.spec.ts`, web units, Playwright `@smoke @regression`
   - **Functional:** Playwright `@functional` (+ module tag `@chat`, `@orders`, …) proving the user journey
6. **Run and confirm PASS:**
   - `pnpm --filter @ekum/web test` / relevant API specs
   - `pnpm test:e2e:smoke` (regression)
   - `pnpm test:e2e:functional` (or filtered module tag)
7. **Trader-eye on the running screen (Required, BM-11).** Green tests are not done. Open the changed flow as a first-time seller (phone viewport). If a client would screenshot one thing as “this looks broken / too loud / I can’t tap it,” that is a **blocker** — fix before claiming done. Tests that only assert the spec you just wrote will not catch this.
8. Pure copy/CSS with no behaviour change may skip new tests — say so explicitly. Still do the trader-eye pass.

## Anti-loophole (Required — green-but-blind)

Playwright/units that pass while clients see obvious holes usually **echo the ticket** instead of locking the product.

1. **Sibling parity assert** — when chrome must match Orders/kit, compare **shared helper output / same class contract** (e.g. Home selected tab ≡ Orders `underlineTabChrome`), not a local “looks selected” regex that would also pass a wrong lime bar.
2. **Edge matrix before code** (Completeness): who · grant · surface · empty/revoke. At least one automated assert per named edge for the slice — not only happy path.
3. **No ticket-echo tests** — a test that only repeats the ticket wording is a BM-11 fail.
4. **Trader-eye is blocking** — if you cannot open the screen, say so; do not call done on green CI alone.
5. **Playwright = journey + one obvious hole** — UI chrome: path + class/helper parity; trust/grants: happy + revoke/deny.

## Bug modes

When fixing a UI bug, add a **regression** test first (BM-* in
`docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-11-quality-gate-and-test-system-design.md`).
